Z||000000||theogre||04-16-2001||11:14 PM||||Folks, Please don't link directly to my fiero cave articles. I know this seems a thing to make life easier but the site isn't set up for that. You will deadend on most pages and that can be very annoying for people. Also I tend to change file names over time as I need to arrange things for administative reasons. A direct link that works today may, literally, break tomorow.<P>I'm not saying all this to be mean or anything. I know the people who do this are just trying to help and I do apreciate that.<P>This is especially true now. I am in the process of a complete rework of the articles to clean up from Word2K and other things. I plan to rearange nearly the entire cave in that process. (I need something to do while I'm out weeks after surgery in may....)<P>The cave has been in constant evolution. No article is ever truely complete. I'm Always adding some small thing or another. (Like the tool part number I threw into the steering column service article last week or so.) Other times I make major changes like the heat management section.<P>(So why don't You "fix" the pages so they won't deadend???? Simple.... Too dam many links to manage. Been there. done that. wasn't remotely fun.)<P>The following lins will always get you to the safe anchors in the cave.<BR> <A HREF="http://theogre.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>http://theogre.shorturl.com</A>  <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>http://fierocave.shorturl.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://theogre.home.sprynet.com" TARGET=_blank>http://theogre.home.sprynet.com</A>  <A HREF="http://theogre.home.sprynet.com/tunnel6" TARGET=_blank>http://theogre.home.sprynet.com/tunnel6</A> <P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||4
